 now retries when the server returns 503. It makes at most 3 attempts in total, and I checked the cases below against a local test server.\n\n**What changed** (`weather.py`):\n- `urllib` raises `HTTPError` on a 503. `get` catches it, waits, and tries again. If the 3rd attempt also gets a 503, that error is passed on to the caller.\n- The waits double each time: 0.5s after the first failure, then 1s after the second.\n- Any other error is raised right away with no retry. That includes other HTTP errors and network errors like timeouts.\n- Two new optional constructor arguments, `max_attempts=3` and `backoff=0.5`, set the number of attempts and the first wait. Existing callers don't need to change.\n\n**Results from the local test server:**\n\n| Server responses | Result | Requests made |\n|---|---|---|\n| 503, 503, 200 | data returned | 3 |\n| 503, 503, 503 | `HTTPError 503` raised | 3 |\n| 500 | `HTTPError 500` raised | 1 |\n| 200 | data returned | 1 |\n\nI didn't add any test files to the repo, because it has none.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 5, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 35011, "requests_cache_write": 143293, "requests_cost_usd": 0.7573952, "requests_count": 5, "requests_input_uncached": 12, "requests_output": 1694, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial30", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 119, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:59:29.681396+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 24.662, "t_checker_s": 2.434, "t_env_setup_s": 0.002, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "none"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", 